<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio da Correggio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1489–1534</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Correggio, Antonio Allegri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio Allegri, known as Correggio after his home town, was an Italian painter of the High <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> who worked mainly in Parma. His dome frescoes in the church of San Giovanni Evangelista and in Parma Cathedral, with figures soaring upwards into light, anticipated baroque ceiling painting. He was also admired for the soft, sensual modelling of his religious and mythological pictures.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-da-correggio.jpg" alt="Antonio da Correggio" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antonio_Allegri_da_Correggio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
